      "side": 1,
      "message": "For 99.9% of the usages you are correct. However, there is one use case where it is not which is why I added this. e.g. We have an APEX that has a java_library \"framework-wifi\" and a service library \"service-wifi\". The \"framework-wifi\" exposes an API for other modules to use (which is why it needs to be converted to a java_sdk_library) but the \"service-wifi\" needs to access implementation specific methods of \"framework-wifi\". It manages to do that at the moment because \"framework-wifi\" is a reference to the implementation library. However, switching it to java_sdk_library makes \"framework-wifi\" resolve to a stubs library.\n\nThis change will ensure that a dependency on the implementation library for a java_sdk_library will only work within an APEX.\n\nAlso, I think having the dependency on the implementation be explicit is clearer.",
